const prevVol = { num: 4, title: 'Desert City Cygnus &amp; Gladiator Trials', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-4/` };
const nextVol = { num: 6, title: 'Granorg Liberation &amp; Shadow of Dias', href: `${baseUrl}walkthrough/volume-6/` };
---

<WalkthroughLayout
  volume={5}
  volumeTitle="Beastkind Stronghold &amp; Skalla Infiltration"
  chapterRange="Chapters 41–50"
  description="Forgia's elder council, Itolia Wasteland skirmishes, uncovering Dias's conspiracy, and Beastkind unification."
  stats={stats}
  quickJumps={quickJumps}
  prevVol={prevVol}
  nextVol={nextVol}
>

  <!-- Chapter 41 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch41"
    number={41}
    title="Cygnus (Standard Chapter 5)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="42" party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Scorching Battlefield">
        <p>After resting at the inn, head west to the plaza, and look for Ricky along the main road. Talk to him to receive the [An Unwanted Reunion] sidequest. Head to the tavern and talk to the green-haired girl, Mimel, twice. Return to the "Chi-Clad Warrior" node and talk to the bartender. Return to the "Scorching Battlefield" node and talk to Mimel again to be prompted for a decision. Choosing to "Capture Mimel" will unlock the [Simmering Fury] ending.</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Otherwise, choosing to "Let Mimel go" will advance [An Unwanted Reunion].  Talk to Ricky again to complete the [An Unwanted Reunion] sidequest and receive the SABLE LARME (DEF+33/MDF+25/MAG+5, equip on Raynie).</p>
      <p>Head up to Cygnus HQ and talk to Garland to be prompted for a decision. Choosing to "Stay in Cygnus" will unlock the [A Mighty King's Death] ending.</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Warlord's Request">
        <p>Instead, return to this node and choose to "Lead the way". After some events, you will receive the BLOODIED ARMLET.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Dias Strikes">
        <p>Return to the "Desert City Messiah" node and proceed with events as before. This time, you will get an extra scene that will unlock the [Hedge in Exile] node. Return to the "Warlord's Request" node, choose to "Lead the way" and events will proceed more favorably this time.</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 42 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch42"
    number={42}
    title="Itolia Wasteland (Standard Chapter 5)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="42" party="Stocke, Eruca, Marco" enemies={[{"name": "Desert Mercenary", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Granorg Blitzer", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Red Granorg Archer"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix title="Traveling Merchant" items={[{"name": "First Aid Kit       400     Bastard Sword", "price": 4000}, {"name": "Tourniquet         1000     Goldy Lance", "price": 4300}, {"name": "Special Tea        1200     Steel Gauntlet", "price": 3400}, {"name": "Holy Water          500     Mueke Knife", "price": 3800}, {"name": "Anti-Poison          50     Solid Slugs", "price": 3800}, {"name": "Anti-Fear            50     Iron Mail", "price": 2400}, {"name": "Anti-Paralytic       50     Chain Kimono", "price": 1900}, {"name": "Anti-Curse           50     Gold Clothes", "price": 3200}, {"name": "Anti-Sleep           50     Iron Breastplate", "price": 6500}, {"name": "Anti-Stone           50     Gold Dress", "price": 5100}, {"name": "Panacea             800     Iron Charm", "price": 2500, "note": "buy 4"}, {"name": "Poison Wing         350     Crystal Charm", "price": 2500, "note": "buy 8"}, {"name": "Sleep Wing          500     Bishop Stud", "price": 3000}, {"name": "Divine Water       1500     Sprig Ring", "price": 5000}]} itemTitle="Inventory" />
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Stocke Strikes">
        <p>To the left is a traveling merchant with new accessories. Buy 8 Crystal Charms for Stocke, Raynie, &amp; Eruca. If you have the money, buy 4 Iron Charms for Rosch &amp; Gafka later. Stocke should pretty much be a full-time mage for the remainder of the game, since his physical attacks don't deal as much damage.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Pieti Edge, Gospel Armor, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Magic Spear, Sable Larme, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Madre Blade, Iron Mail, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> Silver Dagger, Life Robe, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Eruca:</strong> Solid Slugs, Rune Dress, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> Moirae Manteau, 4 Iron Charms</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Secret Weapons">
        <p>Go north to begin taking out the Ballistas. Head right to find a chest which contains 3 SPECIAL TEAS. The other paths are blocked for now, so head west to find your first batch of ballistas. Let's take out the one in the upper left corner first. Then, the one in the lower left corner.</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Ballista, Granorg Blitzer x3" weakness="Fire, Sleep">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> You can use Sleep Gas to crowd control the Blitzers.  If you have enough starting turns, use two Left Assaults and a G-Frost to take them out. Use the Change command to string together all 10 turns.  Have Marco use all of his turns casting Trans-turn on Stocke.  Then, arrange your turns like so: Double Slash, Mana Shot, Double Slash, Mana Shot, Double Slash, Mana Shot, Steal, Steal, Steal, Steal, to boost the combo bonus, hopefully allowing you to steal the FREIKUGEL KREUZ (ATK+4/MAG+35/DEF-3) for Eruca.  Equipping him with the Gospel Armor to boost his Luck will help immensely.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>You can equip Stocke with his Moirae Manteau and hand down the Gospel Armor to Marco after stealing the new gun for Eruca.  Before heading back, check out the well in the area to the west.  Climb down the well to find a chest which contains a CELESTIAL OIL.  The man here appears to have been waiting for you, but won't say why.  Remember that for later.  Return back two screens.</p>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Garland's Arrival">
        <p>Garland will arrive with explosives. Unfortunately, they do not work on the northern barricades, so drag a barrel to blow up the eastern rocks. Go east two screens and search the upper right corner for a hidden chest which contains 3000 G. Head back west, then north, and west a screen to find a chest which contains an IRON CHARM. Return east and head north.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Destroy the Ballistas">
        <p>Search along the upper wall to find a hidden chest which contains the POISONER'S SCROLL for Raynie. Then, take out the two ballista in the upper right and lower right corners, where you can apply the same strategies as the before. Temporarily give Raynie's Crystal Charms to Aht, bring her in to replace Marco, and head back to talk to Garland.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Terrain Advantage">
        <p>With the ballistas destroyed, there's only one more enemy to take care of, as well as an old friend.</p>
      </Callout>
      <BossCard name="Gardner, Palomides" weakness="Lightning">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Use a Magic Herb on Aht and have Eruca cast Regenerate.  Gardner can cast support and healing spells, so you want to take him out first.  I would avoid using the Change command to set up combos, as their attacks can really hurt.  Your main source of damage will be Electric Traps, but don't worry so much about getting both of them onto the same one, as taking out Gardner first. You could steal a Giant Armor from Palomides, but you already have better.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: A New Journey">
        <p>After returning to Cygnus, leave the city to proceed to Chapter 6.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Pieti Edge, Moirae Manteau, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Magic Spear, Sable Larme, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Madre Blade, Gospel Armor, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> Silver Dagger, Life Robe, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Eruca:</strong> Freikugel Kreuz, Rune Dress, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> 5 Iron Charms</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 43 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch43"
    number={43}
    title="Itolia Wasteland (Standard Chapter 6)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="44" party="Stocke, Aht, Eruca" enemies={[{"name": "Black Curtain", "weakness": "Fire"}, {"name": "Cockatrice", "weakness": "Lightning"}, {"name": "Fanatic", "weakness": "Ice"}, {"name": "Grypender", "weakness": "Ice"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>__                          ________
               |1 |         | |            |        |    S - Save Point
               /XX|       __| |            |   MR   |    X - Roadblock
              /XXX|      |     \_____   ___|   RR   |    R - Rocks
             /XXXX|_     |       _ __   ___   ______|    M - Moon Armlet
            /       |    |___   | |        | |           1 - Tungsten Mail
           /       _|        |XX| |
          |       |___   ____|  | |        | |
          |                     | |__   __/S |
          |_       ___   ___    |____   __   |
            \_____/         \   \         \  |
                            |   /          | |
                            |  |           | |
   _____
  |     |  _______          |  |           | |            _____
  |     | |       |         |  |          /   \          /     \
  |_   _| |____   |         |XXX\____   _/     \___   __/       \__
    | |        |  |        /    X
          _____|  |__   __/     X____   __     ____   __         __
    | |__/                     /  __      \___/         \       /
    |____          __   __    |__/  |                    \_____/
         \________/       \         |
                           \       /
                            \   __/
                            |  |</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Waiting at Skalla">
        <p>Before heading to Skalla, we've got a lot of sidequests to do. First, return to Cygnus and talk to Garland to receive the [Moon Armlet] sidequest. Then, head over to the equipment shops. Talk to Hertz &amp; Bram over there to receive [The Good Thief's Way] sidequest. Go back to the Itolia Wasteland.</p>
      </Callout>
      <p>At this point, Aht should have learned Cross Star and Eruca should have learned Blizzard.  If so, you really shouldn't have to worry about using traps for now. Just use Assault and those two spells to deal with all the enemies.</p>
      <p>Return to the well that is north, west, and north one screen from the initial save point.  Go down the well and the man, named Sword, is ready to talk to you now and give you [The Living Legend] sidequest.  Leave the well area, then walk east two screens and north two screens.  You should see a small rock formation in the middle.  Search around there for the hidden MOON ARMLET.</p>
      <p>Head west to find some rocks you'll need to blow away.  Go past them, and west again.  You can find a hidden barrel along the lower cliff that you will need in addition to the two visible ones, in order to get past the rocks to the north, but if you do, you'll be well rewarded with a chest which contains the TUNGSTEN MAIL (DEF+42/MDF+24/SPD-2, equip on Marco).  Save the Gospel Armor for later.  Talk to Garland at Cygnus to complete the [MOON ARMLET] sidequest and receive the SUNA-WATARI (ATK+42/SPD-4, sell).</p>
      <p>Return to "The Beginning" node.  Talk to Wand, the boy at the weapon shop, and choose "Hope" to advance [The Living Legend] sidequest.  While you are here, talk to the child by the tavern to advance [The Good Thief's Way] sidequest.</p>
      <p>Return to "The Messenger's News" node and search the upper right corner for the hidden SHADE PACT for Stocke.  Return to the "Castle Sewers" node.  Talk to a man in the lower left corner named Pentacle, and choose "The Past" to advance [The Living Legend] sidequest.  While you are here, talk to the boy to the left of the inn to advance [The Good Thief's Way] sidequest.</p>
      <p>Return to the "How to Disappear" node, go down the sewers, and head west one screen.  Search the left of the upper paths to find the hidden SUNLIGHT PACT for Eruca.</p>
      <p>Return to "The Beastkind Forest" node and talk to Chalice, the lady by the equipment shop.  Choose "All Things" to advance [The Living Legend] sidequest. Search to the left of the sparkling bushes at the center of town to find the hidden METEORITE PACT for Aht.</p>
      <p>Return to the "Waiting at Skalla" node and talk to Sword at the well to complete [The Living Legend] sidequest.  He will introduce you to Vainqueur, who can teach new abilities to Stocke, Aht, and Eruca.  Talk to him again to receive [The Blades Trial], [The Starlit Trial], [The Light Trial], and [The Three Contracts] sidequests.  If you've followed the walkthrough up to now, you should be able to teach 3 abilities to Stocke, 2 abilities to Aht, and 3 abilities to Eruca.</p>
      <p>Go back to Cygnus and talk to Bram to complete [The Good Thief's Way] and receive the PIERCING SCROLL from Hertz for Raynie.  This would also be a good time to return to "A New Mission" to teach those new scrolls to Raynie.</p>
      <p>When you are ready, return to the Itolia Wasteland.  Simply head straight north and blow up all the rocks along the way to reach the northern exit that will lead you to Skalla.</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 44 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch44"
    number={44}
    title="Skalla (Standard Chapter 6)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="45" party="Stocke, Aht, Eruca" inn="100 G"
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <ShopMatrix title="Skalla (Standard Chapter 6) Merchant" items={[{"name": "Soothing Balm", "price": 100}, {"name": "First Aid Kit", "price": 400}, {"name": "Tourniquet", "price": 1000}, {"name": "Herbal Tea", "price": 350}, {"name": "Special Tea", "price": 1200}, {"name": "Healing Herb", "price": 500}, {"name": "Holy Water", "price": 500}, {"name": "Anti-Poison", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Fear", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Paralytic", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Curse", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Sleep", "price": 50}, {"name": "Anti-Stone", "price": 50}, {"name": "Panacea", "price": 800}, {"name": "Panacea Plus", "price": 2000}, {"name": "Poison Wing", "price": 350}, {"name": "Sleep Wing", "price": 500}, {"name": "Power Down", "price": 500}, {"name": "Might Herb", "price": 500}, {"name": "Divine Water", "price": 1500}]} equipment={[{"name": "Bastard Sword", "price": 4000}, {"name": "Alchemy Edge", "price": 9500}, {"name": "Goldy Lance", "price": 4300}, {"name": "Witch Spear", "price": 4800, "note": "buy for Raynie"}, {"name": "Steel Gauntlet", "price": 3400}, {"name": "Mueke Knife", "price": 3800}, {"name": "Death Dagger", "price": 5200}, {"name": "Solid Slugs", "price": 3800}, {"name": "Iron Mail", "price": 2400}, {"name": "Gold Clothes", "price": 3200}, {"name": "Iron Breastplate", "price": 6500}, {"name": "Running Sand", "price": 3800}, {"name": "Gold Dress", "price": 5100}, {"name": "Shadowrun Dress", "price": 5600}, {"name": "Iron Charm", "price": 2500}, {"name": "Crystal Charm", "price": 2500}, {"name": "Bishop Stud", "price": 3000}, {"name": "Sprig Ring", "price": 5000}, {"name": "Peridot", "price": 1750}, {"name": "Amazonite", "price": 1750}]} itemTitle="Item Shop" equipmentTitle="Equipment Shop" />
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: An Introduction">
        <p>After some initial dialogue, head to the weapon shop to the right where you should buy a Witch Spear for Raynie. Below the weapon shop is a hidden chest which contains the THUNDERSTAR PACT for Aht. Enter the center house to talk to Tarquin again. He will give you the SAND SWORD to advance the [Sand Sword] sidequest and unlock the [Merchant Tarquin] node. Talk to him again to advance the [Mercenary Recruit] sidequest. Head to the inn to meet Eruca's contact.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: To Holff Ruins">
        <p>You will need to pass through the Itolia Wasteland and Abyssia Forest in order to reach the ruins. From the northern entrance of the Itolia Wasteland, head east one screen, south two, and east one. Pass the Gutrals to the east to make it to the Abyssia Forest.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Pieti Edge, Moirae Manteau, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Witch Spear, Sable Larme, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Madre Blade, Tungsten Mail, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> Silver Dagger, Life Robe, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Eruca:</strong> Freikugel Kreuz, Rune Dress, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> Gospel Armor, 5 Iron Charms</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 45 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch45"
    number={45}
    title="Abyssia Forest (Standard Chapter 6)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="45" party="Stocke, Aht, Eruca" enemies={[{"name": "Army Wasp", "weakness": "Ice"}, {"name": "Blom"}, {"name": "Rose Balsam", "weakness": "Fire"}, {"name": "Stompy", "weakness": "Fire"}, {"name": "Wood Fang", "weakness": "Fire"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>| |       S - Save Point
                                 /   \      G - Guard
     ______ ______              |   __|     * - Sneak attacks
    |    G2|      |             |____ |     1 - Beast Charm
    |  _   |3  _  |             |____ |     2 - Roll-Cut Scroll
    | | |1 |  | | |             | ____|     3 - Healing Fruit
    | | |__|__| | |             |___  |     4 - Gaia Blade
    | |         | |                 | |     5 - Tourniquet x2</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>_| |_     ___| |    _______   ___| |                _
  |     |   | ____|   | S    _   ___ *|               |5|
  |____ |   |____ |   |____ |     __| |___   _________| |
  | ____|   |* ___|   |  ___|    |    ____   ___________|
  |____ |   | |       | |        |4  |
  |  ___|   |  \_____/* |        |___|
  | |        \___   ___/
__| |            | |              ____
__  |                            |  __
  | |___   ____  | |        __   | |
  |_____   __  | | |__   __/  \__| |
             | |_|  __   _________*/
             |_____|</pre>
      </AsciiMap>
      <p>Many enemies here are weak to fire, so Stocke's new Wisp Blade can be very useful in the right battles.  Eruca's Burst Light can also be quite obscene. At the fork, head south, then east two screens where you will bump into Liese. Talk to her to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest.</p>
      <p>Return to the entrance and follow the northern path to the next screen until you reach an open area.  In the lower left corner is a chest which contains a BEAST CHARM (ATK+10) that you should save for later.  Examine the corpse in the upper right corner to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest.  Open the hidden chest next to him which contains the ROLL-CUT SCROLL for Marco.  Return to Liese once more to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest.</p>
      <p>I would strongly recommend leaving and completing some sidequests at this time, since the rewards are really good, and the next couple areas are a little tough.  Return to "A New Mission" to teach that new scroll to Marco and to "The Three Contracts" to teach the new Pact to Aht.  Return to the "Echoing Hills" node and defeat the bandits again.  Talk to Tarquin to advance the [Mercenary Recruit] sidequest.</p>
      <p>Return to the "Castle Sewers" node and talk to Liese in the northwest corner of the Downtown area to be prompted for a decision.  Choosing to "Leave it to her" will unlock the [Chains of Hatred] ending.  Instead, return to the decision point and choose to "Believe in him" to advance the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest.  Talk to the soldier by the save point on Main Street to complete the [Mankind &amp; Beastkind] sidequest and receive the PROMISED KNIFE (ATK+27/MAG+75/HP-30, equip on Aht).  Aht should now be able to one shot almost everything with her Cross Star spell.</p>
      <p>Return to "The Resistance" node and talk to Will, giving him the Sand Sword and receiving 1500 G.  Like with the Escort event earlier, you don't have to do it now, but if you don't, you will have to do it sooner or later anyway.  This will also enable you to unlock two rather obscure nodes, as well.</p>
      <p>Continue the plot to the "Capital in Flames" node at Granorg.  Walk north until you automatically talk to Will to unlock the [Will's Sword] node.  Return to the "Wounded Otto" node and continue the plot through the Sand Fortress to unlock the [Will to the Rescue] node.</p>
      <p>Return to the "Waiting at Skalla" node and proceed to Skalla, as before.  Talk to Tarquin to advance the [Mercenary Recruit] sidequest.  Proceed with events as before until you make it back to the Abyssia Forest.</p>
      <p>Follow the lower path east one screen to a fork.  If you like, head east to see how Liese's relationship is going.  Otherwise, head north.  Follow the left path to the next area where there is a chest which contains a HEALING FRUIT. Go back to the fork and take the right path to the next area.</p>
      <p>There is another fork ahead.  After clearing the enemies, search behind the trees on the lower left side for a barrel.  Move it down to the rocks along the lower path to gain access to another small area.  Search around for a hidden chest which contains the GAIA BLADE (ATK+30/MAG+25/HP+100, equip on Marco).</p>
      <p>Continue east to a long road of tall grass.  At the end of the path is a dead end with a chest which contains 2 TORNIQUETS.  Return to the last fork and follow the northern path to the ruins.  You should rest up at Skalla before entering, first.</p>
      <Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
        <p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>
        <strong>Stocke:</strong> Pieti Edge, Moirae Manteau, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Raynie:</strong> Witch Spear, Sable Larme, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Marco:</strong> Gaia Blade, Tungsten Mail, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Aht:</strong> Promised Knife, Life Robe, Bishop Stud x3<br/>
        <strong>Eruca:</strong> Freikugel Kreuz, Rune Dress, Crystal Charm x3<br/>
        <strong>Extra:</strong> Gospel Armor, Beast Charm, 5 Iron Charms</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 46 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch46"
    number={46}
    title="Holff Ruins (Standard Chapter 6)"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="47" party="Stocke, Aht, Eruca" enemies={[{"name": "Glascol", "weakness": "Lightning"}, {"name": "Ice Tail", "weakness": "Fire"}, {"name": "Iron Shell", "weakness": "Poison/Fire"}, {"name": "Kenpo Master", "weakness": "Sleep"}, {"name": "Living Rock", "weakness": "Lightning"}, {"name": "Magus"}, {"name": "Monk"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
      <AsciiMap>
<pre>_|D|_                   S - Save Point        P - Floor Panel
