      </AsciiMap>
      <p>Finally, return to the four-way intersection and take the left path.  Proceed up the steps to the left, and search above for a hidden chest which contains a CELESTIAL DEW.  Go back down the steps and up through another tiny, dark passage until you reach a wide open area.  Search the center of the area for a hidden chest which contains the DIVINE PACT for Eruca.  Head right along the path to a tiny room with a chest which contains a DIVINE WATER.</p>
      <p>Return to the open area and take the upper path to the next room.  Follow path up, then left two rooms to a fork.  The lower path leads to an isolated chest which contains 2 SPECIAL TEAS.  Go back to the fork, and follow the right path until you reach a + shaped area.  At the top is another floor panel with a switch that will open the door above.  I would strongly recommend having two maxed out Mana Burst gauges before moving on.  Then, return to the save point and head up to find the Beast Mark and your next test.</p>
      <BossCard name="Shadow" weakness="Fire">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Have Eruca cast Magic Boost on Aht.  Have her lay Flamestar Traps in the back row.  Then use Push Assault and Right Assault to defeat him quickly.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <p>For defeating him, you will win the BEAST MARK.  That's it.  Everything's done. Might as well pack our bags and go home.  Or I could be speaking too soon.</p>
      <BossCard name="Guardian" weakness="None">
        <p><strong>Strategy:</strong> Another giant spider, except this one can kill you in one turn.  This is why I recommended having your maxed out Mana Burst gauges.  Use two of them to use Turn Break on its first two turns, giving you nine consecutive turns. Stocke should lead by using a Magic Herb on Eruca for casting G-Frost.  This is where Aht will really shine.  Her new Dancing Death ability can REALLY drive up the combo bonus.  Arrange the remaining 8 turns as follows: Dancing Death, Fire, Dancing Death, Fire, Dancing Death, G-Frost, G-Frost, G-Frost to defeat the Guardian.</p>
      </BossCard>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Overcoming the Trial">
        <p>With the Beast Mark, you could get past the roadblock in Alternate History, but since we're almost done here, we might as well wrap things up. Talk to Bergas to be prompted for a decision on how to assault Granorg. Choosing to "Lead the way" will unlock the [Premature Invasion] ending.</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Final Defense">
        <p>Before moving on, return to Historia with the Beast Mark to unlock your final Mana Burst. Return to "The Three Contracts" and teach the new Pact to Eruca. Then, return to the previous decision point, choose to "Wait for the Gutrals", and events will proceed more favorably this time.</p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

